campaign-component: party-arrival-and-first-day-response

LOCKED: The party arrives approximately twenty minutes after the initiating event.

James

LOCKED: James confesses to causing the initial hotel attack and immediately begins closing Gates.

LOCKED: James can close most unsupported random Gates rapidly.

LOCKED: Maintained Gates resist closure and may reopen while their far-side anchors or maintainers remain active.

Bramble

LOCKED: Bramble creates an approximately 30-metre-radius area that extinguishes fires.

LOCKED: She flies through the city at approximately 40 miles per hour.

WORKING CALCULATION: In ideal continuous coverage, she can clear approximately 3.9 square kilometres per hour, but her strategically important function is creating firebreaks, suppressing advancing fronts, protecting hospitals and command centers, and breaking large conflagrations into fires that Furui Tokyo’s systems can manage.

D

LOCKED: D establishes a healing station.

LOCKED: D can heal one person per second for up to 80 HP after SPAA.

WORKING CALCULATION: Maximum throughput is 3,600 patients per hour or 86,400 patients in twenty-four hours, although transport and triage are the real limits.

Dweia

LOCKED: Dweia establishes a second healing station using Circle Magic.

LOCKED: Dweia’s healing circle can regrow lost limbs.

LOCKED: This allows rescue crews to use emergency amputation when necessary to free trapped victims without condemning them to permanent disability.

Meerkat Robots

LOCKED: A large number of meerkat robots perform triage, locate survivors, and transport injured people to D and Dweia.

LOCKED: Their work is essential to exploiting the otherwise impossible throughput of the two healing stations.

Will

LOCKED: Will controls the weather to direct tritium, smoke, and airborne contamination away from major population concentrations.

LOCKED: Will can also reduce wind-driven fire spread, preserve aerial visibility, and protect reservoirs and evacuation zones.

Aragorn

LOCKED: Aragorn coordinates with Furui Tokyo’s government, military, rescue organizations, hospitals, and local superhuman defenders.

LOCKED: His primary contribution is restoring a coherent metropolitan command network and integrating party capabilities with local response systems.

Aiden

LOCKED: Aiden uses Force telekinesis to remove rubble from trapped survivors.

LOCKED: His best use is precise extraction based on meerkat-robot triage data rather than general debris clearing.
